  "body_excerpt": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - Ethernet bonding driver;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - F2FS file system;\n  - Tracing infrastructure;\n  - io_uring subsystem;\n  - Networking core;\n  - IUCV driver;\n  - RxRPC session sockets;\n(CVE-2022-49149, CVE-2022-49170, CVE-2022-49182, CVE-2022-49201,\nCVE-2024-53187, CVE-2024-53210, CVE-2024-56763, CVE-2026-43456,\nCVE-2026-52910)",
